<title>BULGARIA: Bulgaria places 1.978 bln levs of 6-mth T-bills.</title>
<headline>Bulgaria places 1.978 bln levs of 6-mth T-bills.</headline>
<dateline>SOFIA 1996-09-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>Bulgaria's Finance Ministry placed a special issue of six-month floater coupon T-bills with a total par of 1,977.625 million levs, yielding 224.85 percent, the Bulgarian National Bank (BNB) said.</p>
<p>The coupon of the issue was set equal to the BNB's central interest rate (CIR) for the period to maturity. The CIR is now set at an annual 108 percent.</p>
<p>In line with its usual practice the BNB did not specify with which financial institutions the issue was placed.</p>
<p>Details of the issues follow:</p>
<p> Issue number		BG 3018196025</p>
<p> Par value		   1,977.625 million levs</p>
<p> Issue date		  Sept 11, 1996</p>
<p> Maturity date	     March 12, 1997</p>
<p> Selling price	     85.50 pct</p>
<p> Yield to maturity	 79.94 pct</p>
<p>Cumulative annual yield 224.85 pct</p>
<p>-- Sofia Newsroom, (++359-2) 981 8569</p>
